{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cat .agents/skills/q-agent/SKILL.md; cat .agents/skills/q-agent/skills/q-ci-fixer/SKILL.md; cat /home/iquantum/.codex/plugins/cache/engram/engram/0.1.5/skills/memory/SKILL.md'","aggregated_output":"---\nname: q-agent\ndescription: >\n  Master project orchestrator by Gabriel Magallón Sánchez (Quantum). Activate on: \"start agent\",\n  \"launch q-agent\", \"/q-agent\", \"new project\", \"new feature\", \"audit code\", or any\n  start-of-cycle trigger. Guides Steps 0–3 (one question at a time), then coordinates\n  execution via Dual Engine (Gentle-AI Integrated ODD vs q-agent Standalone) in Steps 4–7.\n  Enforces Article ARQ-01: Vertical Slices by default, template hygiene (.html embed),\n  zero-mock terminal evidence, and minimal indirection. Tool-agnostic.\nauthor: Gabriel Magallón Sánchez / QuantumEdu (Quantum)\nversion: 2.9.2\nlicense: Apache-2.0\nsources: [chat]\naliases: [agente, /q-agent, iniciar agente, dev agent, orchestrator]\nmetadata:\n  context_policy: \"PROGRESSIVE\"\n  requires: [\"references/execution-authority.md\", \"templates/CONSTITUTION.md\"]\n  may_call:\n    - \"skills/q-deliberate\"\n    - \"skills/q-grill-me\"\n    - \"skills/q-adversarial-review\"\n    - \"skills/q-ci-fixer\"\n    - \"skills/q-audit-readonly\"\n    - \"skills/q-delegate-context\"\n    - \"skills/q-session-wrap\"\n    - \"skills/q-gbrain-assistant\"\n---\n\n# q-agent v2.9.2 — Master Project Orchestrator\n\n> **Filosofía Fundamental:** **CONCEPTS > CODE • DUAL-ENGINE RESILIENCE • MINIMAL INDIRECTION • TERMINAL EVIDENCE GATE • DEPLOY GOVERNANCE • VERTICAL SLICES**  \n> Director de Orquesta Senior (GDE & MVP). Guía Pasos 0–3 (una pregunta por turno), ejecuta Pasos 4–7 bajo **Artículo Constitucional ARQ-01** (Slices ~400 LOC), formaliza el Gate de Despliegue en Paso 8 con firma humana, y canaliza producción en Paso 9.\n\n## 1. Quick Bootstrap & Triggers\n- **Cuándo Aplica**: Iniciar proyectos (Plan A), features/brownfield (Plan B), parches quirúrgicos ≤3 archivos (Plan F), auditorías forenses (Plan C).\n- **Cuándo NO Aplica (Anti-Triggers)**:\n  - Ediciones de un solo archivo obvias sin ambigüedad (usar edición directa inline).\n  - Tareas de solo lectura sin solicitud de ciclo o plan (usar `skills/q-audit-readonly`).\n  - No deliberar si la decisión técnica ya fue resuelta o delegada explícitamente.\n- **Protocolo Bilingüe**: Detecta y refleja el idioma del usuario. Artefactos técnicos (código, commits, specs) **siempre en inglés**.\n- **Fronteras de Directorio**: `<SKILL_ROOT>` (paquete `q-agent`) vs `<PROJECT_ROOT>` (repositorio activo/`cwd`). Nunca mezclar.\n\n## 2. Contrato de Ejecución del Ciclo (Pasos 0 a 9)\n\n```text\nPasos 0–2 ──► MODO SOCRÁTICO GUIADO (1 pregunta por turno, esperar respuesta)\nPaso 3     ──► GATE DUAL-ENGINE (Gentle-AI ODD vs Standalone ODD)\nPasos 4–7  ──► EJECUCIÓN ODD (Bitácora viva, Slices ~400 LOC, Evidencia Terminal + Adversarial)\nPaso 8     ──► DEPLOY GATE (REVIEW.md compilado, firma humana obligatoria)\nPaso 9     ──► BUCLE OPS-TO-ODD (Reproduction-First ante incidentes)\n```\n\n### [Paso 0] Selección de Plan y Onboarding\n- [ ] Preguntar únicamente si el plan no fue resuelto:\n  - `[A] Greenfield` (nuevo sistema) | `[B] Brownfield` (evolución) | `[F] Fast-Track` (patch ≤3 archivos) | `[C] Audit` (forense CAB-RP 2.0).\n\n### [Paso 1] Contexto Inicial (1 Pregunta por Turno, luego STOP)\n- [ ] Indagar datos faltantes: Nombre/módulo, problema central que resuelve y restricciones (stack, BD, integraciones).\n\n### [Paso 2] Deliberación y Elicitación\n- [ ] **2a (Arquitectura incierta)**: Invocar `skills/q-deliberate` solo ante disyuntivas reales no delegadas.\n- [ ] **2b (Memorias persistentes)**: Cargar `references/context-retrieval.md` solo para hechos faltantes concretos.\n- [ ] **2c (Plan A Supuestos)**: Invocar `skills/q-grill-me` para desafiar supuestos no validados antes de diseñar specs.\n\n### [Paso 3] Gate de Metaorquestación (Dual Engine)\n- [ ] Sondear: `gentle-ai --version 2>/dev/null || echo \"GENTLE_AI_NOT_FOUND\"`.\n  - **Motor A (Gentle-AI ODD)**: Si está presente. Bitácora en `odd/tasks/<feature>.md`, CodeGraph prioritario.\n  - **Motor B (Standalone ODD)**: Si falta. Bitácora en `q-tasks/<feature>.md`, CodeGraph CLI / herramientas locales.\n- [ ] **CodeGraph Auto-Init**: Si falta índice en repo: `test -d .codegraph || codegraph init -y`. Exploración obligatoria vía MCP `codegraph_explore` o CLI upstream (`codegraph explore/impact`) antes de búsquedas ciegas.\n- [ ] Verificar `CONSTITUTION.md` (Artículo ARQ-01: Slices por defecto, SQLite WAL, higiene HTML, SQL parametrizado, cero mocks). En proyectos nuevos sin constitución, inicializar con `python3 tools/q-checklist/q_checklist.py`.\n\n### [Paso 4] Apertura de Bitácora Única ODD\n- [ ] Crear bitácora viva instanciando `templates/task-log-template.md`.\n- [ ] Definir User Stories (`US-xx`) y Acceptance Criteria (`UAC-xx`). Tabla `Terminal Evidence Gate` inicialmente vacía.\n- [ ] For resumable local execution, use [Local task recovery](references/local-task-recovery.md): register task IDs, run authorized finite commands, and record verification after committing. On a resumed session inspect `q-agent resume`; never replay uncertain work without inspecting effects and explicit retry authority. Machine verification does not replace acceptance or human gates.\n\n### [Paso 5] Implementación por Slices Verticales\n- [ ] Construir slice por slice (Storage ──► Handler ──► Template `.html`).\n- [ ] Aislar en Git Worktree si hay concurrencia: `python3 tools/q-worktree/q_worktree.py create --task TASK-XX`.\n- [ ] ⛔ **BLOQUEO**: Prohibido marcar tareas como completadas (`[x]`) en este paso.\n\n### [Paso 6] Dual Verification Gate (Terminal Evidence + Adversarial Review)\n- [ ] **Autonomous E2E**: Follow [Hosted unattended E2E repair](references/unattended-e2e.md). Freeze tests, run real E2E, diagnose failures and invoke q-ci-fixer for at most TWO total correction rounds per task (initial run + up to two reruns). Persist the shared counter across P06/review/P07; exhausted budget means BLOCKED, never a reset. Require regressions and independent APPROVED review before completion.\n- [ ] **Fase A (Máquina)**: Compilación, linters, tests reales y smoke HTTP.\n- [ ] **Fase B (Adversarial)**: Despachar `skills/q-adversarial-review` en subagente aislado (`invoke_subagent`).\n  - Auditar diff contra ARQ-01 con protocolo **Review Remembers** (`R-IDs`).\n  - Exigir veredicto `APPROVED` antes de autorizar cierre.\n- [ ] **Registro en Bitácora**: Registrar salida exitosa (exit 0) en la tabla `Terminal Evidence Gate`.\n- [ ] Marcar checkbox `[x]` únicamente con evidencia terminal registrada y veredicto `APPROVED`.\n\n### [Paso 7] Higiene Determinista, Consolidación y Cierre\n- [ ] Ejecutar linters oficiales. Si falla: invocar `skills/q-ci-fixer` (máximo 2 pasadas).\n- [ ] Consolidar nuevo Slice en `BLUEPRINT.md` (Sección 3.1).\n- [ ] **Si Plan C (Auditoría Forense)**: Ejecutar obligatoriamente `workflows/plan-c-audit.md` (Atomic Dispatch C1 a C5).\n- [ ] Cierre de sesión local-first: Invocar `skills/q-session-wrap`.\n\n### [Paso 8] Gate de Despliegue y Autorización Humana\n- [ ] Evaluar blast radius con Merge Gate: `python3 tools/q-merge-gate/q_merge_gate.py --base main --head HEAD`.\n  - Exit 0 (`PROCEED`) | Exit 7 (`HUMAN_APPROVAL_REQUIRED` si >500 LOC/billing/auth) | Exit 8 (`HUMAN_ACTION_REQUIRED` si DDL/migraciones).\n- [ ] Compilar evidencia de P06, P07 y veredicto en artefacto versionado `REVIEW.md`.\n- [ ] ⛔ **BLOQUEO ABSOLUTO**: Prohibido ejecutar despliegue a producción sin firma humana explícita en chat.\n\n### [Paso 9] Bucle Ops-to-ODD (Producción)\n- [ ] Inyectar telemetría de fallos reales (Sentry/logs) ejecutando `prompts/P10_ops_to_odd.md`.\n- [ ] **Reproduction-First**: Crear test unitario/integración que falle (`RED_FAIL`) antes de autorizar cualquier fix.\n\n## 3. Completion Gate del Orquestador\nAntes de certificar la entrega de un ciclo al usuario:\n- [ ] Cada tarea de la bitácora viva cuenta con entrada verificada en `Terminal Evidence Gate`.\n- [ ] Veredicto adversarial emitido como `APPROVED` sin blockers `R-xx` abiertos.\n- [ ] `REVIEW.md` generado y presentado para firma humana en Paso 8.\n- [ ] Estado final declarado explícitamente: `[COMPLETE]`, `[BLOCKED - reason]` o `[FAILED - reason]`.\n\n## 4. Referencias y Workflows Bajo Demanda\n- **Protocolo Plan C (Auditoría Forense)**: `workflows/plan-c-audit.md` (Despacho atómico en 5 fases).\n- **Protocolo Dual Engine**: `references/dual-engine.md`.\n- **Mapeo de Planes (A, B, F, C)**: `references/plans.md`.\n- **Autoridad de Ejecución**: `references/execution-authority.md`.\n- **Plantillas Vivas**: `templates/CONSTITUTION.md`, `templates/BLUEPRINT.md`, `templates/task-log-template.md`.\n---\nname: q:ci-fixer\ndescription: \"Trigger: /q-ci-fixer, /fix-ci, arreglar ci, fallo github actions, reparar test linteo, coverage gate fail, resolver pyright ruff. Diagnostica y repara quirúrgicamente fallos en pipelines de CI/CD (ruff, eslint, pyright, tsc, pytest, deno test) sin debilitar las reglas ni reducir los umbrales de cobertura.\"\nlicense: Apache-2.0\nmetadata:\n  author: QuantumEdu\n  version: \"2.0.0\"\n  date: \"2026-10-10\"\n  context_policy: \"COMPACT\"\n  requires: [\"CI logs or test failure output\"]\n  produces: [\"Surgical CI Fix\", \"Exit 0 Local Verification\"]\n---\n\n# q:ci-fixer v2.0 — Reparación Quirúrgica de CI/CD\n\n## 1. Quick Bootstrap & Triggers\n- **Propósito**: Diagnosticar y corregir fallos en pipelines de CI/CD (GitHub Actions, linters, types, tests) de forma sistemática y quirúrgica, devolviendo el build a verde.\n- **Cuándo Aplica**:\n  - Un workflow de CI falló en un PR o commit reciente.\n  - Pasos de linteo (`ruff`, `eslint`, `flake8`) o análisis de tipos (`pyright`, `tsc`, `mypy`) arrojaron errores.\n  - La suite de pruebas falló por aserciones rotas (`AssertionError`) o por caer bajo el umbral de cobertura.\n- **Cuándo NO Aplica (Anti-Triggers)**:\n  - ⛔ **PROHIBIDO debilitar contratos**: Jamás editar `ci.yml` o configuraciones para bajar el porcentaje de cobertura ni silenciar con `# noqa` / `# type: ignore` / `eslint-disable`.\n  - ⛔ **PROHIBIDO refactors cosméticos o nuevas features**: Modificar únicamente las líneas indispensables para resolver el error.\n  - No usar si el fallo responde a una falta de definición de producto o cambio arquitectónico no acordado.\n- **Límite Duro**: Máximo **2 pasadas de corrección**. Si persiste cualquier fallo en la 2da pasada, detenerse y declarar bloqueo.\n- **Hosted autonomous E2E**: Follow [unattended E2E](../../references/unattended-e2e.md). Diagnose real logs, increment the durable correction counter BEFORE editing, preserve tests/thresholds and rerun the exact failing E2E command. Share TWO total rounds across P06, review and P07 for the same task; never reset on invocation. Missing prerequisites or uncertain side effects require diagnosis, not blind retry.\n\n## 2. Contrato de Ejecución Paso a Paso (4 Capas)\nEn E2E autónomo, antes de M1 comprobar e incrementar el presupuesto compartido.\nLimitar autofix y formato a fuentes autorizadas, excluyendo tests congelados;\ncualquier modificación invalida evidencia y revisión anteriores y exige repetirlas.\n- [ ] **M1 (Linteo y Formato Automático)**:\n  - Python: `uv run ruff check --fix <archivos>` y `uv run ruff format <archivos>`.\n  - JS/TS: `pnpm eslint --fix <archivos>` y `pnpm prettier --write <archivos>`.\n- [ ] **M2 (Tipado Estático y Firmas)**:\n  - Resolver `None` no manejados mediante guardas tempranas (`if val is None: return`).\n  - Corregir anotaciones asegurando coincidencia con la firma de dominio.\n- [ ] **M3 (Aserciones de Tests)**:\n  - Si es regresión de código: reparar lógica en el componente de producción.\n  - Si cambió legítimamente la regla de negocio: actualizar el test autorizado.\n- [ ] **M4 (Cobertura de Ramas)**:\n  - Agregar casos de prueba unitarios específicos para bifurcaciones (`if/else`, `except`) no cubiertas.\n\n## 3. Completion Gate\nAntes de declarar resuelto el CI:\n- [ ] Ejecutar localmente el comando exacto que falló en CI y verificar **código de salida `0`**.\n- [ ] Comprobar que `ci.yml` y umbrales de cobertura permanecen inalterados.\n- [ ] Estado final declarado:\n  - `[COMPLETE]` ──► Build local pasando en verde con exit code 0.\n  - `[BLOCKED - reason]` ──► Error requiere decisión humana de arquitectura o se agotó el límite de 2 pasadas.\n  - `[FAILED - reason]` ──► Imposible resolver sin debilitar contratos.\n---\nname: engram-memory\ndescription: \"ALWAYS ACTIVE — Persistent memory protocol. You MUST save decisions, conventions, bugs, and discoveries to engram proactively. Do NOT wait for the user to ask.\"\n---\n# Engram Persistent Memory — Protocol\n\nYou have access to Engram, a persistent memory system that survives across sessions and compactions.\nThe agent MUST follow this protocol without waiting for activation.\n\n## AVAILABLE TOOLS\n\nUse the Engram tools actually exposed by Codex, with their registered names.\nThe names below are logical names; availability and discovery follow Codex's\nhost-specific tool interface, not a universal bootstrap or deferred-tool split.\n\n- `mem_save`, `mem_search`, `mem_context`, `mem_session_summary`\n- `mem_get_observation`, `mem_save_prompt`, `mem_current_project`, `mem_judge`, `mem_compare`\n\n- `mem_update`, `mem_review`, `mem_pin`, `mem_unpin`, `mem_suggest_topic_key`\n- `mem_session_start`, `mem_session_end`, `mem_doctor`, `mem_capture_passive`\n\n## PROACTIVE SAVE TRIGGERS (REQUIRED — do NOT wait for the user to ask)\n\nCall `mem_save` IMMEDIATELY and WITHOUT BEING ASKED after any of these:\n\n### After decisions or conventions\n- Architecture or design decision made\n- Team convention documented or established\n- Workflow change agreed upon\n- Tool or library choice made with tradeoffs\n\n### After completing work\n- Bug fix completed (include root cause)\n- Feature implemented with non-obvious approach\n- Notion/Jira/GitHub artifact created or updated with significant content\n- Configuration change or environment setup done\n\n### After discoveries\n- Non-obvious discovery about the codebase\n- Gotcha, edge case, or unexpected behavior found\n- Pattern established (naming, structure, convention)\n- User preference or constraint learned\n\n### After user confirmation or rejection\n- User confirms a recommendation you made (\"go with that\", \"let's do that\", \"sounds good\", \"agreed\", \"perfect\", or the equivalent in the user's language)\n- User rejects an option or approach (\"no, better X\", \"not that one\", or the equivalent in the user's language)\n- User expresses a preference (\"I prefer X over Y\", \"always do it this way\", or the equivalent in the user's language)\n- User makes a decision after you presented tradeoffs or options\n- A discussion concludes with a clear direction chosen — even if the agent proposed it\n\n### Self-check — ask yourself after EVERY task:\n> \"Did I or the user just make a decision, confirm a recommendation, express a preference, fix a bug, learn something non-obvious, or establish a convention? If yes, call mem_save NOW.\"\n\nFormat for `mem_save`:\n- **title**: Verb + what — short, searchable (e.g. \"Fixed N+1 query in UserList\", \"Chose Zustand over Redux\")\n- **type**: bugfix | decision | architecture | discovery | pattern | config | preference\n- **scope**: `project` (default) | `personal` | `global`\n- **topic_key** (optional but recommended for evolving topics): stable key like `architecture/auth-model`\n- **content**:\n  **What**: One sentence — what was done\n  **Why**: What motivated it (user request, bug, performance, etc.)\n  **Where**: Files or paths affected\n  **Learned**: Gotchas, edge cases, things that surprised you (omit if none)\n\n### Topic update rules (REQUIRED)\n\n- Different topics MUST NOT overwrite each other (example: architecture decision vs bugfix)\n- If the same topic evolves, call `mem_save` with the same `topic_key` so memory is updated (upsert) instead of creating a new observation\n- If unsure about the key, call `mem_suggest_topic_key` first, then reuse that key consistently\n- If you already know the exact ID to fix, use `mem_update`\n\n## WHEN TO SEARCH MEMORY\n\nWhen the user asks to recall something — any variation of \"remember\", \"recall\", \"what did we do\",\n\"how did we solve\", or the equivalent in the user's language, or references to past work:\n1. First call `mem_context` — checks recent session history (fast, cheap)\n2. If not found, call `mem_search` with relevant keywords (FTS5 full-text search)\n3. If you find a match, use `mem_get_observation` for full untruncated content\n\nAlso search memory PROACTIVELY when:\n- Starting work on something that might have been done before\n- The user mentions a topic you have no context on — check if past sessions covered it\n- The user's FIRST message references the project, a feature, or a problem — call `mem_search` with keywords from their message to check for prior work before responding\n\n## DELIVERY GUARANTEE\n\nMemory operations are internal bookkeeping, never the user-facing answer. Complete required memory work before composing the completed-task reply; send the complete answer as the final message of the turn with no later tool calls. If memory work fails or needs follow-up, still send the answer.\n\n## SESSION CLOSE PROTOCOL (REQUIRED)\n\nBefore ending a session or saying \"done\" / \"that's it\", you MUST:\n1. Call `mem_session_summary` with this structure:\n\n## Goal\n[What we were working on this session]\n\n## Instructions\n[User preferences or constraints discovered — skip if none]\n\n## Discoveries\n- [Technical findings, gotchas, non-obvious learnings]\n\n## Accomplished\n- [Completed items with key details]\n\n## Next Steps\n- [What remains to be done — for the next session]\n\n## Relevant Files\n- path/to/file — [what it does or what changed]\n\nThis is NOT OPTIONAL. If you skip this, the next session starts blind.\nSummary persistence does not end the session. Codex's SessionEnd hook owns\nlifecycle closure independently of the agent's summary.\n\n## PASSIVE CAPTURE — adapter-specific safety net\n\nWhen completing a task or subtask, include a \"## Key Learnings:\" section with\nnumbered items. Automatic capture is adapter-specific: Codex's SubagentStop hook\nforwards eligible delegated/subagent output for server-side extraction. Ordinary responses\nfrom the main agent are not automatically captured by this hook; the section alone\ndoes not guarantee storage. Use `mem_save` as the primary path for significant,\nverified knowledge.\n\nExample:\n## Key Learnings:\n\n1. bcrypt cost=12 is the right balance for our server performance\n2. JWT refresh tokens need atomic rotation to prevent race conditions\n\nYou can also call `mem_capture_passive(content)` directly with any text that contains a learning section.\nThis explicit extraction path is a safety net, not a replacement for `mem_save`.\n\n## AFTER COMPACTION\n\nIf you see a message about compaction or context reset, or if you see \"FIRST ACTION REQUIRED\" in your context:\n1. IMMEDIATELY call `mem_session_summary` with the compacted summary content — this persists what was done before compaction\n2. Then call `mem_context` to recover any additional context from previous sessions\n3. Only THEN continue working\n\nDo not skip step 1. Without it, everything done before compaction is lost from memory.\n\n## Codex session binding\n\nCodex registers the native PreToolUse command `engram hook codex-pre-tool-use`\nfor `mcp__engram__mem_*` and `mcp__plugin_engram_engram__mem_*`. For supported\nEngram write/session tools, it resolves the authoritative Codex host session to\nthe server-confirmed Engram identity before binding arguments: `session_id` for\nwrites and `id` for session start/end. `mem_session_end` uses `id`, not `session_id`.\nDo not invent or override this identity. Read-only tools are unchanged; malformed\ninputs or unconfirmed host resolution deny mutating calls.\n\nThe lifecycle hook also supplies the confirmed identity after registration or\nrenewal. For direct/nonintercepted clients, reuse this exact identity as\n`session_id` for attributed writes (`mem_save`, `mem_save_prompt`,\n`mem_session_summary`, `mem_capture_passive`), and as `id` for `mem_session_end`.\nNever reconstruct a resume suffix or guess an ID when confirmation is missing.\n\n**Fallback**: If tools are unexpectedly unavailable, run `engram setup codex`\nand restart Codex. Setup repairs Codex's authoritative `[mcp_servers.engram]`\nregistration; use the actual tool names exposed by Codex.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
